Azure Hosting Handoff for LucidPM and Portfolio Manager

Goal

Prepare both applications to run in Microsoft Azure using the same Azure subscription while keeping the applications, databases, configuration, and data separate.

Primary goals:

Keep Azure cost at or near $0.

Preserve the existing application architectures as much as possible.

Avoid unnecessary database rewrites.

Allow both applications to run under separate subdomains of an existing domain.

Keep local development working while cloud deployment is built and tested.

Do not make destructive changes to the current local production environments.

Target Azure Architecture

Azure Subscription

One shared Azure subscription.

Resource Group

Use one shared resource group unless there is a strong technical reason not to.

Suggested name:

Lucido-Apps-RG

Container Apps Environment

Use one shared Azure Container Apps Environment.

Deploy two separate Container Apps:

LucidPM

Portfolio Manager

Each app must have:

Its own container configuration.

Its own environment variables.

Its own secrets.

Its own database connection strings.

Its own custom domain.

Its own authentication configuration if enabled.

Domains

Use separate subdomains.

Example:

lucidpm.example.com

portfolio.example.com

Do not assume control of the root domain is required.

Azure Container Apps should handle HTTPS using Azure managed certificates.

Database Architecture

Use Azure SQL Database.

Do not convert either application to PostgreSQL.

Use one Azure SQL logical server if practical.

Create separate databases:

TenantCRM

TenantCRM_Test

PortfolioManager

PortfolioManager_Test

Each application must continue to treat production and test databases separately.

Azure SQL Free Tier Goal

Configure databases to use the Azure SQL free offer where eligible.

The current Azure offer provides a free allowance per qualifying database.

Configure databases so they pause or stop consuming paid resources when the free allowance is exhausted rather than automatically generating unexpected charges, if Azure still offers that option during setup.

Container Apps Free Tier Goal

Both apps will share the Azure Container Apps free allowance at the subscription level.

Configure both apps to scale to zero when idle.

These are low-usage applications, so the target is to stay within the shared free compute allowance.

Avoid provisioning always-on infrastructure unless required.

Do not provision Azure Container Registry automatically.

Azure Container Registry is not free.

Prefer a deployment/image approach that avoids adding a paid registry unless there is a clear need.

