Authentication and Security

Both applications will become internet-accessible.

Do not expose them publicly without evaluating authentication.

These applications contain sensitive business and financial information.

Portfolio Manager may contain particularly sensitive financial and personal information.

Consider Azure Container Apps built-in authentication using Microsoft Entra ID.

Prefer infrastructure-level authentication if it avoids unnecessary custom authentication code.

Do not implement a new authentication system without first evaluating Azure's built-in option.

Deployment Separation

Although both apps may share Azure infrastructure, they must remain independently deployable.

LucidPM deployment must not restart or replace Portfolio Manager.

Portfolio Manager deployment must not restart or replace LucidPM.

Each app should have:

Independent container image.

Independent revision history.

Independent environment variables.

Independent ingress.

Independent health status.

Independent custom domain.

Independent secrets.

Independent database credentials where practical.

